WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.420
A group class now holds one live link to the ride hub, and only while you ride it.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.632
Join a group session and the app opens one connection to the hub, signed in with

00:00:14.632 --> 00:00:15.632
your session.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.053
It asks the hub for its time five times and keeps the quickest answer, so every

00:00:28.053 --> 00:00:29.636
rider's clock agrees.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.707
If the link drops, it tries again at once, then after two, five and ten seconds,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.637
then every thirty, and checks the clock again.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.863
Ride alone, or just browse, and there is no connection at all.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.862
The ride looks the same on every screen, with the link held quietly underneath.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.096
What the tests prove: one connection, a measured clock, a quick return, and nothing

00:01:17.096 --> 00:01:17.978
left open.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
